# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Added in Phase 1, when `npm run format:check` became a blocking CI gate
# (.github/workflows/lint-and-format.yml). A gate is only worth having if it
# fails for real reasons, so anything the formatter should not own is excluded
# here rather than being reformatted to satisfy it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Prose. These documents are hand-wrapped at 80 columns and read as prose;
# prettier reflows markdown tables and list continuations, which would produce a
# large diff with no reader-visible benefit. PROJECT_LIFECYCLE.md is additionally
# append-only by its own stated rule, so reformatting past phases is exactly the
# edit that file forbids.
*.md

# Committed benchmark output. Machine-written evidence behind the latency claims,
# already marked linguist-generated in .gitattributes. Reformatting it would
# change bytes a reviewer is meant to be able to diff against a re-run.
#
# Globbed across every phase directory rather than named one at a time: the v0
# fingerprint was listed explicitly, so the v1 runner's fingerprint failed the
# blocking format:check the first time a phase directory appeared. Same mistake
# .gitattributes had, same fix.
benchmarks/**/results/
benchmarks/*/environment.json

# FROZEN MEASUREMENT INSTRUMENT — see BENCHMARKING.md.
# baseline.js is the script the v0 numbers were produced with, and the v0-vs-v1
# comparison is only valid while it stays the same instrument. Formatting is not
# behaviour, but a formatter that rewrites this file on a whim is one more way for
# it to drift, so the tool is simply not allowed to touch it. The realistic-mix
# and saturation scripts are not frozen and are formatted normally.
benchmarks/k6/baseline.js
